# Swift quality gates (executable companion to guardrails-compliance)

When you add or edit **Swift** (`.swift`) files, prove the org Swift guardrails still hold
before finishing. This rule supplies **commands**; threshold **numbers** live in
`docs/guardrails/swift/profile.thresholds.yml` (consumer overlay
`config/swift.profile.thresholds.yml`). Policy and deviations:
[guardrails-compliance.mdc](guardrails-compliance.mdc). Proposed IDs:
[`docs/new-guardrails/swift.md`](../../docs/new-guardrails/swift.md).

## Prefer local CI parity

```bash
PIXELDIVE_REQUIRE_SWIFT=1 bash scripts/check-ios-sdk.sh
```

Linux hosts without Swift skip unless `PIXELDIVE_REQUIRE_SWIFT=1` (SWIFT-ENV-001;
proposed overlay allows Foundation-only `swift test` on Linux). The SwiftUI demo
still needs Xcode.

## Per-gate fallback (map to Guardrail IDs)

| Check | Typical command | Guardrail |
|-------|-----------------|-----------|
| Format | SwiftFormat with `ios/.swiftformat` | SWIFT-ENV-002, SWIFT-LINT-001 |
| Lint | SwiftLint with `ios/.swiftlint.yml` | SWIFT-LINT-001, proposed SWIFT-CPLX-001 |
| Tests | `swift test --package-path ios` | SWIFT-TEST-001 |
| Line coverage | Xcode / llvm-cov; no branch key | SWIFT-TEST-002 |
| Docs | Doc comments on public API | SWIFT-DOC-001 |

Cite the Guardrail ID in the PR when a gate fails or when recording a deviation.

## Design habit

Keep `PixeldiveClient` on Foundation/`URLSession`. Map iOS device APIs into the
existing Android JSON keys; put native iOS fields in `metadata`. Prefer `struct`
Codable models (proposed SWIFT-API-004 / KT-API-001).
